# mm.fs.shell

mm.shell.full's IoService and FileService over mm.fs, so the full-profile
interpreter's redirections, pathname expansion, and file tests reach any
mounted volume: a directory, littlefs, FAT, or 9P. FileServices owns the files
it opens, eight at a time, and hands the interpreter handles to them; handles
it did not open -- the standard streams -- and pipes go to a base IoService
the caller supplies, and without one are Invalid. Relative paths resolve
against a directory the caller sets, "/" by default, since mm.fs has no
working directory.
